(5) driving a motor vehicle transporting explosives, flammable and explosive chemical substances, and highly toxic, radioactive, and other hazardous materials, failing to travel at the designated time, route, and speed, or failing to hang warning signs and take necessary safety measures;
(6) driving a motor vehicle transporting oversized indivisible items, failing to travel at the designated time, route, and speed, or failing to hang warning signs;
(7) driving a motor vehicle transporting hazardous chemicals entering areas where the passage of hazardous chemical transport vehicles is restricted without approval;
(8) driving a motor vehicle failing to pass in accordance with traffic light indications;
(9) driving a motor vehicle during the period when the motor vehicle driver's license is detained or withheld;
(10) fleeing after causing a traffic accident resulting in minor injury to a person or property damage, which does not yet constitute a crime;
(11) driving a motor vehicle illegally occupying the emergency lane on an expressway or urban expressway.
Article 11: A motor vehicle driver who commits one of the following traffic violations shall be assessed 3 points at a time:
(1) driving a school bus, highway passenger transport bus, tourist passenger transport bus, or other passenger motor vehicle with more than 7 seats, carrying passengers exceeding the approved number by twenty percent or more but less than fifty percent;
(2) driving a motor vehicle other than a school bus, medium-sized or larger passenger and freight motor vehicle, or hazardous materials transport vehicle on roads other than expressways or urban expressways at a speed exceeding the prescribed speed by twenty percent or more but less than fifty percent;
(3) driving a motor vehicle on an expressway or urban expressway failing to drive in the prescribed lane;
(4) driving a motor vehicle failing to overtake or yield in accordance with regulations, or driving in the wrong direction on roads other than expressways or urban expressways;
(5) driving a motor vehicle, when overtaking while preceding motor vehicles are stopped in a queue or moving slowly, occupying the opposite lane or weaving among waiting vehicles;
(6) driving a motor vehicle engaging in acts that hinder safe driving, such as making or answering handheld phone calls;
(7) driving a motor vehicle passing through a crosswalk failing to slow down, stop, or yield to pedestrians in accordance with regulations;
(8) driving a motor vehicle failing to yield to a school bus in accordance with regulations;
(9) driving a freight motor vehicle carrying goods exceeding the maximum permitted total mass by thirty percent or more but less than fifty percent, or carrying passengers in violation of regulations;
(10) driving a motor vehicle with license plates not installed in accordance with regulations on the road;
(11) after a vehicle breaks down or is involved in an accident and stops on the road, failing to use lights or set up warning signs in accordance with regulations;
(12) driving a highway passenger transport bus, tourist passenger transport bus, or hazardous materials transport vehicle that has not undergone regular safety technical inspections as required on the road;
(13) before driving a school bus on the road, failing to check whether the school bus condition meets safety technical requirements, or driving a school bus with safety hazards on the road;
(14) driving a freight motor vehicle continuously for more than 4 hours without stopping for rest, or with a rest period of less than 20 minutes;
(15) driving a motor vehicle on an expressway at a speed lower than the prescribed minimum speed.
Article 12: A motor vehicle driver who commits one of the following traffic violations shall be assessed 1 point at a time:
(1) driving a school bus, medium-sized or larger passenger and freight motor vehicle, or hazardous materials transport vehicle on roads other than expressways or urban expressways at a speed exceeding the prescribed speed by ten percent or more but less than twenty percent;
(2) driving a motor vehicle failing to meet oncoming vehicles in accordance with regulations, or failing to reverse or make a U-turn in accordance with regulations on roads other than expressways or urban expressways;
(3) driving a motor vehicle failing to use lights in accordance with regulations;
(4) driving a motor vehicle violating the indications of prohibitory signs or prohibitory markings;
(5) driving a motor vehicle carrying goods with length, width, or height exceeding the prescribed limits;
(6) driving a freight motor vehicle carrying goods exceeding the maximum permitted total mass by less than thirty percent;
(7) driving a motor vehicle other than a highway passenger transport bus, tourist passenger transport bus, or hazardous materials transport vehicle that has not undergone regular safety technical inspections as required on the road;
(8) driving a freight motor vehicle with unauthorized changes to its registered structure, construction, or characteristics on the road;
(9) when driving a motor vehicle on the road, the motor vehicle driver failing to wear a seat belt in accordance with regulations;
(10) driving a motorcycle without wearing a safety helmet.
Chapter 3: Execution of Point Assessment
Article 13: The public security organ traffic management department shall assess points for traffic violations of motor vehicle drivers at the same time as making an administrative penalty decision.
Before making a penalty decision against a motor vehicle driver, the department shall, at the same time as informing of the proposed administrative penalty decision, inform of the point assessment value for the traffic violation, and shall record it in the penalty decision letter.
Article 14: If a motor vehicle driver has two or more traffic violations subject to point assessment, the point values shall be accumulated.
A motor vehicle driver may handle records of multiple traffic violations of the same motor vehicle at one time, with point values accumulated. If the accumulated points are less than 12, they may handle records of traffic violations of other motor vehicles they drive; if the accumulated points reach 12, they shall not handle records of traffic violations of other motor vehicles.
Article 15: When a scoring cycle expires, if a motor vehicle driver's accumulated points are less than 12, the points within that scoring cycle shall be cleared; if the accumulated points are less than 12 but there are fines overdue and unpaid, the point values for traffic violations within that scoring cycle for which fines have not yet been paid shall be transferred to the next scoring cycle.
